<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="1d078e19">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        It is necessary to plan for a potential no-go decision at any of the decision points during the cutover phase
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The contingency plan establishes how to delay the system go-live date or how to proceed with limited functionality
        or restricted scope
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The contingency plan may also outline a detailed roll-back plan which would allow the company to reactivate the
        legacy system and continue daily business on that system
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="e0279c4b"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="bd2b4d27"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="60632266">&lt;p&gt;
    The contingency may be an interim state that will be operated until a proper failover environment is configured or the
    previous state can be restored and may entail the service being unavailable until a more permanent solution is ready.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
